"""The service logos the launcher can draw, and the words that reach them.

Homepage fetches these from an icon repository. This page cannot: a container
has no promise of reaching the internet, and a panel is the one screen where
nobody can open a console to find out why a picture did not load. So they are
carried in the image instead -- one path apiece, drawn as inline SVG, tinted
either in the brand's own colour or in the theme's ink when that colour would
disappear against the panel.

The paths come from **simple-icons** (https://simple-icons.org), which places
them in the public domain under CC0 1.0. The marks themselves remain the
trademarks of the services they identify, and they are used here for what
trademarks are for: saying which service a tile opens.

Prime Video is the one on the asked-for list that is not here -- simple-icons
does not carry it -- so `prime-video` is a name in the ordinary icon list and
gets a television.

Each entry is a slug, the words that should reach it in both languages, the
brand colour, and the path itself on a 24x24 grid.
"""

